<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Jobs, inflation key to rates outlook-RBA.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Jobs, inflation key to rates outlook-RBA.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) governor Bernie Fraser said on Thursday that Australia's jobs performance and inflation would be important factors influencing the interest rate outlook over the next six to 12 months.</p>
<p>Asked what would influence rates over the next six to 12 months, Fraser told a parliamentary committee: &quot;How the assessments of what's happening to employment and unemployment develop and that of course depends on how the growth in the economy unfolds and that in turn depends upon a whole lot of things.&quot;</p>
</text>
